Real Government Workflow Exception Real-world Example: Business Permit Processing
Business permit renewal at the BPLO (VLAN 130) needs access to property assessment from the Assessor (VLAN 40) and tax clearance 
from the Treasurer (VLAN 30). Since this is a real LGU process, these connections are allowed as specific, limited exceptions to the default-deny rule.
* Permit: VLAN 130 (BPLO) → VLAN 40 (Assessor) — TCP, application port only
* Permit: VLAN 130 (BPLO) → VLAN 30 (Treasurer) — TCP, application port only
* Deny: everything else between Zone D and Zone C, implicit

Layer 2 Hardening
* Port security on all access ports (max 1 MAC addresses per port, violation = shutdown) prevents unauthorized device plug-ins, common in a public-facing government building.
* DHCP snooping on all user VLANs — blocks rogue DHCP servers, trusts only the uplink to the real DHCP server.
* Dynamic ARP Inspection (DAI) — prevents ARP spoofing/man-in-the-middle within a VLAN, paired with DHCP snooping.
* BPDU Guard on access ports — protects against accidental or malicious switch loops from someone plugging in an unmanaged switch.

